.TH ELITEIPC 7 "2026-09-24" "ELITEIPC 1.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
eliteipc \- ownership, deployment and failure model of ELITEIPC shared-memory IPC
.SH DESCRIPTION
ELITEIPC is a C11 CPU-to-CPU transport with SPSC and publish-first NCQ-SC64
queues, fixed payload blocks, explicit zero-copy leases, and application-owned
lifecycle management. It does not require a daemon or third-party native
runtime. The optional Python binding adds a CPython exporter and ctypes
calling interface, not a second queue algorithm.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.nf
SPSC:
  producer -- payload then release(P) --> acquire(P) -- consumer
  producer <-- acquire(C) <-- release(C) after final consumer read

NCQ-SC64:
  QF -> producer owns block -> construct -> publish completed ID -> QR
  QF <- return after final read <- consumer owns block <---------- QR

Management (not a payload path):
  authority -> constructed grants -> registered process cohort
  suspect -> retire/quarantine -> distinct successor -> fenced disposal
.fi
.PP
QF and QR entries contain packed generation/index identities, not heap
pointers. Reserve a payload before constructing it; never hold a blocking
ready-queue position while user serialization runs. A paused publisher after
entry installation leaves consumable data and helpable tail bookkeeping.
.SH INVARIANTS
.TP
.B Exclusive ownership
Every block is free, ready, exclusively held, transfer-owned or retained as
uncertain responsibility. Historical array words are not additional live
membership. Phase values alone are not allocation or recovery oracles.
.TP
.B Publication
All required payload and metadata writes happen-before authorized reads
through the correct release/acquire handoff.
.TP
.B Reclamation
Every valid read alias ends before the release/acquire chain authorizes
physical overwrite by a later producer. A mapping kept alive without its
token kept reserved is not sufficient.
.TP
.B Linearization
NCQ entry-install CAS publishes. Successful head CAS removes. Tail help is
subsequent bookkeeping. A former owner must not touch a block after its
transfer linearizes, even before the original function returns.
.TP
.B Identity
No live generation resets or wraps counters, packed cycles, lease epochs or
one-shot grant identities. Library version and wire ABI are distinct.
.TP
.B Lifetime
Atomic construction precedes exposure. No concurrent truncation,
reinitialization, unmapping or old-address redirection is permitted.
.SH LAYOUT
LE128-V1 has 2048-byte mode-specific headers, a 512-byte immutable prefix,
128-byte descriptor/entry cells, 256-byte participant records and a
16384-byte format quantum. Relative offsets permit unrelated mapping bases.
Runtime bounds, canonical strides, CRC and compiled atomic representations
are checked before normal operations.
.PP
Alignment isolates designated independent cells on admitted cache-line
granularities. It cannot eliminate true sharing on one NCQ cursor, cache-set
conflicts, prefetch traffic, CPU migration, or OS scheduling disturbances.
The format is not a huge-page request or a GPU/DMA coherence protocol.
.SH OPERATIONAL ENVELOPE
Use trusted, registered participants on the same live host. Serialize each
endpoint and the authority. End all aliases before transfer. Provide a
schedulable authority and bounded application backpressure. A caller that
retains a lease indefinitely consumes its capacity indefinitely.
.PP
SPSC polling try operations have the bounded algorithmic path defined by the
admitted primitive model. NCQ is a lock-free reference, not wait-free for each
caller. Empty/full observations are not scheduling errors by themselves.
Per-caller starvation and long wall-clock delays remain possible.
.PP
The native baseline supports Linux and macOS. The optional experimental
FreeBSD profile is POLL_ONLY and must pass its own native CI. An x86 Linux
build, an ARM assembly listing, or a VM test is not native M3 Max evidence.
.SH SIGNAL AND CRASH POLICY
SIGKILL cannot execute cleanup. SIGSTOP is not death; signal delivery is
not terminal wait evidence. Keep signal handlers out of queue, allocator,
printf and cleanup code. Normal execution must handle interrupted OS calls.
.PP
Retirement prevents new cooperative admission, but does not cancel every
already admitted CAS. A committed old-generation message may remain pending
when a successor starts. Classify it as pending or uncertain, not delivered.
.PP
A timeout is suspicion. Do not reclaim a slot solely because its epoch or
heartbeat appears old. A resumed process can still write through its existing
pointer. Retain old backing, establish holder quiescence or terminal fencing,
and use a physically distinct successor without redirecting old aliases.
.PP
The manager bounds storage at four objects and two quarantines. Exhausting
that budget rejects admission rather than silently leaking unlimited
replacements. Authority failure, unknown descendants, host power loss and
malicious shared writes are separate failure domains.
.PP
The supplied chaos harness targets only its owned children. It reconciles
final free/ready/retained partitions after terminal quiescence. It does not
scan live ordinary descriptor bytes and reconstruct a supposedly safe owner.
.SH PERFORMANCE REPORTING
A performance record names the exact CPU/OS/compiler, timer, payload,
participants, placement, workload, repetition and measurement interval.
RTT is request construction through response validation and return; RTT/2 is
not a direct one-way measurement. Inverse throughput is not latency.
.PP
The interactive demo shows directional Mmsg/s (two payload records per RTT)
and exact window p50/p99 instrumented RTT. It has one outstanding request,
no warmup or core pinning, and includes clock/read/validation work. Console
and evidence output occur between windows and can perturb later windows.
It is a demonstration, not the preregistered latency qualification lane.
.PP
The full benchmark tools retain raw ticks and exact message membership.
Sanitizer, profiler and scheduling-hook results are never reported as
production-speed measurements. PMCs are distinct from elapsed-time clocks;
CNTVCT is not retired core cycles. Unsupported counters remain unavailable.
.SH VERIFICATION AND CI
The distribution separates artifact admission, finite control/handoff
models, native concurrent tests, sanitizers, throughput, latency, counters,
and chaos. Seven finite model spaces were exhausted in the retained formal
campaign; larger configured spaces and external model-checker refinement
remain separately documented. A finite run is not all future executions.
.PP
GitHub CI is correctness and build automation on hosted resources, not a
machine-independent performance acceptance gate. TSan is scoped to a
single-process, one-mapping thread adapter. Valgrind does not prove the
shared-memory ownership protocol. FreeBSD QEMU is a guest portability lane,
not bare-metal hardware qualification. Review action pins and transitive VM
image/tool downloads before enabling untrusted pull requests.
.SH BUILD AND INSTALL
.nf
cmake -S . -B build/cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build/cmake --parallel 2
cmake --install build/cmake --prefix /your/versioned/prefix

# Existing GNU Make pipeline:
make CC=clang libraries python demo
make CC=clang release-check check-seeding
.fi
.PP
CMake exports elite::ringbuffer and any built elite::ringbuffer_static or
elite::ringbuffer_shared targets. C++ consumers use the opaque C interface.
Install into a fresh version-specific prefix, not over loaded libraries.
The optional Python package is built by the existing Make target with its
matching interpreter headers; it is not hidden inside the CMake export.
.SH INTEGRITY AND PUBLICATION
SHA-256 manifests bind bytes, not author identity or executed hardware.
The sealed Turn 15 archive and the Turn 16 seeding derivative have different
hashes even though their library version is the same. Never force-move a
published tag or replace an existing release asset silently.
.PP
Homebrew/vcpkg recipes are seeding material. Their presence does not imply
acceptance in a public package registry. Bind a reviewed public source URL
to the actual downloaded archive digest before distribution. No signing key,
GitHub secret, remote Git tag or published repository is created by this kit.
